1-b037e258-aa3f-4812-9c3b-291d5f33eeca"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"75f7036a0cf6fb0fbe2f6e0b45d637b7504125bc2039c4b0c6329f24c47771a8","event_uuid":"1cd17155-d8f1-4e36-b658-5275ac2ff0c0","position":{"commit_sha":"f24048a76c2f824ad252ed90307ca299c23aa09b","position":"1788857718099997001-1cd17155-d8f1-4e36-b658-5275ac2ff0c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: Verified-0 voting REJECTED (limbo without auto-rerun); CI concurrency groups REJECTED (serializes a dozen in-flight changes). Approved direction: step-level retry of transport faults INSIDE the CI job + explicit infrastructure fault, not your change message on retry exhaustion; local pre-push import-convention check acceptable if it adds no new ratchet mechanism.","timestamp":1788761551442027001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (2026-09-07): the defect is not missing import-convention guards; the existing guards already catch forbidden imports, but only when invoked through the bare pytest console-script path that omits the checkout root from sys.path. Developers running targeted checks with python -m pytest get a false green because cwd is injected onto sys.path, so tests-rooted imports resolve locally and only fail later under make test/CI's bare pytest. The appropriate fix is visibility/routing through the documented pre-push path and in-test warnings, without adding another AST scan, matching the handoff constraint and the recorded operator ruling.","timestamp":1788847032685662001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation note: chose the fast lint-adjacent path by adding an import-convention make target that runs the existing convention tests with the bare pytest console script, then wiring it into check and verify. This makes the guard harder to miss without adding a new AST scan or duplicating the upcoming ruff TID251 work.","timestamp":1788847761379077001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788575404841209001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8e1184f7-40e1-42e1-9cfb-f3fefe7cc5a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"724c-a725-d5f0-4ffc"}],"description":"## The gap\n\nTwo DIFFERENT tickets hit the same `sys.path` divergence on 2026-09-04/05, hours apart, in\nopposite directions:\n\n- `7f46-790d-7b9f-4db1` — a test module resolved its import only because some earlier-collected\n  test had already put `scripts/` on `sys.path`. It passed under `python -m pytest` and failed\n  under the BARE `pytest` console script.\n- change 2647 (`ff4a-2832`, op-cert binding) — a new test used a `tests.`-rooted import. It passed\n  locally under `python -m pytest` and failed in CI under the bare console script, costing a\n  **23-minute** gating cell and a full re-push, on a queue that was already saturated.\n\nThe rule is real and the guards exist (`tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py`) and they WORK — the second case was caught exactly\nas designed. The problem is WHERE it was caught.\n\n## Why it costs a full CI cycle\n\n`python -m pytest` puts the current directory on `sys.path`; the bare `pytest` console script does\nnot. `make test` and CI use the bare script. So a developer or agent who verifies with\n`python -m pytest` — the more common habit, and the form that works for almost everything else —\ngets a green that CI will not reproduce, and learns about it 23 minutes later from a `Verified -1`.\n\nThe full local contract, `make verify`, DOES catch it, but it costs 20-25 minutes and is documented\nas a once-before-push step. The cheap check is a couple of seconds:\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py\n\nrun with the BARE console script. Nothing points anyone at it at the moment they need it.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than filing under \"read the docs\"\n\nThe failure is invisible at the point of the mistake and expensive at the point of discovery, which\nis the worst possible ordering. It also selects against the careful: an agent that runs a targeted\nsubset before pushing (rather than the full 25-minute suite) is exactly the one this catches out.\nTwo independent instances in a single night is enough evidence that habit is not going to fix it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The cheap import-convention check is named in the documented pre-push path, with the\n      explicit warning that it must be run with the BARE `pytest` console script and that\n      `python -m pytest` cannot detect this class at all.\n- [x] The distinction is stated where the mistake is made — a comment or docstring in each\n      convention test saying, in one line, why `python -m pytest` shows a false green.\n- [x] A developer following the documented pre-push path catches a `tests.`-rooted import before\n      pushing. Proven by deliberately introducing one, running the documented path, and observing\n      it fail — not by asserting the docs now mention it.\n- [x] Consider (decide either way, with a reason recorded) whether the guards should ALSO run under\n      a fast lint-adjacent target so the check is unavoidable rather than remembered.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"adds a bare-pytest import-convention target and wires it into check/verify so the cheap guard is named in the pre-push path and fast-fails before the full suite"},{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"documents the pre-push import-convention guard and explicitly warns that python -m pytest can false-green tests-rooted imports"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py","reason":"adds the in-test warning requested by the ticket for the tests-rooted import convention guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py","reason":"adds the in-test warning requested by the ticket for the scripts import convention guard"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","724c-a725-d5f0-4ffc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b037e258-aa3f-4812-9c3b-291d5f33eeca","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1424-6646-de3f-4264","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Import-convention violations are invisible under python -m pytest and only surface 23 minutes later as a CI Verified -1: two independent instances in one night","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8190abb8-d56c-43d9-b8d2-31da6f9669e6","8259ec8d-07ba-426f-990c-c3c9c3c4ab44","effab4d0-f2d0-4ca2-82c5-5891f89a6144","83706a71-de23-4f06-894e-cb41030237c2","f865d4a2-9c0f-4947-ad04-1bd2ebcdada2","819079b1-419b-4d67-bc43-46bbca8c21a7","bbe31e1e-b715-4708-8f7b-19b3b96c8f05","8e1184f7-40e1-42e1-9cfb-f3fefe7cc5a9","2553b1c1-010a-40fd-9709-fcaebfceb965","b037e258-aa3f-4812-9c3b-291d5f33eeca","1cd17155-d8f1-4e36-b658-5275ac2ff0c0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788870019363325001,"uuid":"9b40ced4-121f-4a1d-b061-abe485a25328"}